# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env (already in .gitignore).
#
# HackerOne API auth uses Basic auth with an API username + token.
# The HACKERONE_API_KEY env var accepts either format:
#   1. "username:token"       (will be base64-encoded for Basic auth)
#   2. A pre-encoded base64 token
#
# Get yours at: https://hackerone.com/users/<you>/api_tokens
#
# Safety reminder (enforced in src/safety.ts):
#   - All API calls are READ-ONLY by default.
#   - Write operations require explicit --allow-write AND an env tagged
#     HACKERONE_ALLOW_WRITE=1.
#   - --mock-api forces the in-memory mock client and skips all live calls.
#
HACKERONE_API_KEY=username:token-goes-here

# Optional: GCP project id where HACKERONE_API_KEY is stored as a secret.
# When set, src/api/key-source.ts will fall back to:
#   gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=HACKERONE_API_KEY --project=$GCP_PROJECT
# This lets CI fetch the key without writing it to disk.
GCP_PROJECT=ruv-dev

# Optional: explicit write-allow flag. Defaults to off.
HACKERONE_ALLOW_WRITE=0
